 "verdict": "Signal at ~29.43 d is reproduced at modest significance (my box depth 365-404 ppm, empirical SNR 7.4-7.9) but is NOT the top blind BLS peak (3:2 alias wins, SDE 7.6 vs 6.8), is detrending-dependent (SDE at 29.433 falls to 3.5-4.0 with 0.5 d or 2 d windows), and ~1/3 of the depth comes from two ~2-3 ppt post-gap systematics (BKJD 231.5 ramp, 937.9 step). With those two cadence groups removed the depth is 185-271 ppm at SNR 3.9-4.8. Per-year depths are inconsistent (Y1 808+-107 vs Y2 168+-101 ppm with a 3 h box). Not a candidate on current evidence; needs the two gap events excised, a gap-aware rerun, and pixel localisation before any further step."
